#!/usr/bin/env python3
#Student Planner
#===============
#A tkinter student planner that can pull your class timetable from a university
#timetable service over a URL.

#Most universities (and Moodle, Canvas, Blackboard, Syllabus+, Scientia,
#MyTimetable, Outlook/Google calendar exports, etc.) publish a personal
#calendar subscription link in the standard iCalendar (.ics) format. Paste that
#link (https:// or webcal://) into the "Timetable Sources" tab and the app
#will download and parse it in the background.

#Features
#--------
#* Weekly timetable view built from one or more timetable URLs
#* Recurring classes (RRULE: DAILY / WEEKLY / MONTHLY / YEARLY, BYDAY, COUNT, UNTIL, EXDATE)
#* Task / assignment tracker with due dates, courses, priority, done flag
#* "Next up" banner, overdue highlighting
#* Offline cache: the last downloaded timetable is stored locally
#* Optional auto-sync on startup, optional request headers (e.g. a token)
#* Unlimited calendar URLs: yours plus classmates' shared calendars, each with an
#  owner (Me / Classmate), a colour, and a show/hide switch
#* Study Group Planner: pick several calendars and find the times when everyone is free

#Only the Python standard library is used. Python 3.9+ recommended.
#Data is stored in  ~/.student_planner.json


